  "question": {
    "text": "Which of the following will precipitate first when aqueous solution containing sulphate ions are added?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Mg}^{2+}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Sr}^{2+}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\mathrm{Ba}^{2+}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Down the group solubility of sulphate decreases. Thus, $\\mathrm{Ba}^{2+}$ ions will precipitate out most easily."
